  "id": "DrugBank_DB00579 - MONDO_19182",
  "verbalization": "Mazindol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Monogenic Obesity through a series of indirect pathways involving obesity disorders. The evidence suggests that Mazindol is associated with Obesity Disorder, which in turn is linked to two different drugs—Fenfluramine and Orlistat—both of which are indicated for Monogenic Obesity. This indicates that Mazindol may act as a mediator in the development of Monogenic Obesity, possibly through the influence of these drugs. The shared association with Obesity Disorder suggests a potential role in the pathophysiology of the condition, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Obesity Disorder highlights the complexity of the relationship, and further research is needed to elucidate the precise role of Mazindol in this context.",
